---
title: Skeleton
category: Components
description: Show the shape of content while it loads with theui-svelte's Skeleton component, in text, rectangle and circle variants.
dir: ".lib/pages"
tags: [skeleton, placeholder, loading, shimmer, component, svelte, svelte-5, theui-svelte, component-library, ui, tailwindcss]
---

<script lang="ts">
  import DocLayout from "#lib/ui/doc/DocLayout.svelte";
  import DocHead from "#lib/ui/doc/Head.svelte";
  import DocBlock from "#lib/ui/doc/Block.svelte";
  import Code from "#lib/ui/doc/CodeBlock.svelte";
  import Example from "#lib/ui/doc/Example.svelte";
  import ConfigComponent from "#lib/ui/doc/ConfigComponent.svelte";
  import { processID, editURL } from "#lib";
  let { component }: {component: any } = $props();

  import { Skeleton } from "theui-svelte";

  let loading = $state(true)
</script>

<DocLayout>
  <DocHead title="Skeleton" text="The Skeleton component stands in for content that has not arrived yet. Instead of an empty area or a spinning circle, the page already shows the shape of what is coming, so nothing jumps when the data lands." edit_url={editURL("skeleton")} />

  <DocBlock title="Example">
    <p class="not-prose">Import the component and give it the size of the thing it replaces. The default variant is a rectangle.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="w-full">
          <Skeleton />
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<script>
  import { Skeleton } from "theui-svelte";
</script>

<Skeleton />
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Variants">
    <p class="not-prose">The <code>variant</code> prop takes <code>rect</code> (default), <code>circle</code> for avatars, and <code>text</code> for lines of writing.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4">
          <Skeleton variant="rect" class="h-16" />
          <Skeleton variant="circle" />
          <Skeleton variant="text" />
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<Skeleton variant="rect" class="h-16" />
<Skeleton variant="circle" />
<Skeleton variant="text" />
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Text Lines">
    <p class="not-prose">With <code>variant="text"</code>, the <code>lines</code> prop draws a paragraph. The last line is shorter, the way a real paragraph ends. Each line takes the line height of its parent, so the placeholder matches the text that will replace it.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-6">
          <Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} />
          <div class="text-2xl">
            <Skeleton variant="text" lines={2} />
          </div>
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} />

<!-- The line height comes from the parent -->
<div class="text-2xl">
  <Skeleton variant="text" lines={2} />
</div>
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Animation">
    <p class="not-prose">The <code>animation</code> prop takes <code>pulse</code> (default), <code>wave</code> for a shimmer that travels across, and <code>none</code> for a still placeholder.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4">
          <Skeleton animation="pulse" class="h-10" />
          <Skeleton animation="wave" class="h-10" />
          <Skeleton animation="none" class="h-10" />
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<Skeleton animation="pulse" class="h-10" />
<Skeleton animation="wave" class="h-10" />
<Skeleton animation="none" class="h-10" />
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Size and Shape">
    <p class="not-prose">Size comes from your own classes, so any width, height or aspect ratio works. The <code>rounded</code> prop sets the corner radius of the <code>rect</code> and <code>text</code> variants.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4">
          <Skeleton class="h-8 w-40" rounded="full" />
          <Skeleton class="aspect-video w-full max-w-sm" rounded="xl" />
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-8" />
            <Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-12" />
            <Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-16" />
          </div>
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<Skeleton class="h-8 w-40" rounded="full" />
<Skeleton class="aspect-video w-full max-w-sm" rounded="xl" />

<Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-8" />
<Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-12" />
<Skeleton variant="circle" class="size-16" />
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Card Placeholder">
    <p class="not-prose">Put a few skeletons together to stand in for a whole card. Match the real layout as closely as you can, so the page does not move when the content arrives.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-xl bg-secondary p-4">
          <Skeleton animation="wave" class="mb-4 aspect-video w-full" rounded="lg" />
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <Skeleton variant="circle" animation="wave" class="size-10" />
            <div class="grow">
              <Skeleton variant="text" animation="wave" lines={2} />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<div class="w-full max-w-sm rounded-xl bg-secondary p-4">
  <Skeleton animation="wave" class="mb-4 aspect-video w-full" rounded="lg" />
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <Skeleton variant="circle" animation="wave" class="size-10" />
    <div class="grow">
      <Skeleton variant="text" animation="wave" lines={2} />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Swapping in Content">
    <p class="not-prose">Show the skeleton while the data is on its way and the real content once it arrives. Mark the area that is loading with <code>aria-busy</code>, so assistive technology knows the content is not final.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="w-full">
          <button class="mb-4 rounded-md bg-brand-500 px-3 py-1 text-on-brand" onclick={() => loading = !loading}>
            {loading ? "Show content" : "Show skeleton"}
          </button>
          <div aria-busy={loading}>
            {#if loading}
              <Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} />
            {:else}
              <p class="not-prose">The real content is here now. It takes the same space as the placeholder, so nothing jumps.</p>
            {/if}
          </div>
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<script>
  let loading = $state(true)
</script>

<div aria-busy={loading}>
  {#if loading}
    <Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} />
  {:else}
    <p>The real content is here now.</p>
  {/if}
</div>
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Customization">
    <p class="not-prose">The <code>class</code> prop sets the size and the colour of the placeholder, and <code>lineClasses</code> styles every line of the <code>text</code> variant.</p>
    <Example>
      {#snippet example()}
        <div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4">
          <Skeleton class="h-10 bg-brand-500/20" />
          <Skeleton class="h-10 bg-info-200 dark:bg-info-900" animation="wave" />
          <Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} lineClasses="h-3 rounded-full" />
        </div>
      {/snippet}
      {#snippet code()}

```html
<Skeleton class="h-10 bg-brand-500/20" />
<Skeleton class="h-10 bg-info-200 dark:bg-info-900" animation="wave" />
<Skeleton variant="text" lines={3} lineClasses="h-3 rounded-full" />
```
      {/snippet}
    </Example>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Accessibility">
    <p class="not-prose">A skeleton is decoration, so it is hidden from screen readers with <code>aria-hidden</code>. What matters is the area around it: put <code>aria-busy="true"</code> on the container while it loads, and remove it once the content is there. Announce the result in a live region if the wait is long. For people who prefer reduced motion both animations stop by themselves, leaving a plain placeholder.</p>
  </DocBlock>

  <DocBlock title="Configuration">
    <ConfigComponent {component} />
  </DocBlock>

